# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference copy of the block added to the TEST server's Caddyfile, which lives
# in the BACKEND repository (bookeat1/backend, deploy/Caddyfile) and on the host
# at /opt/bookeat/deploy/Caddyfile.
#
# It is kept here so the frontend deploy is reproducible from this repository
# alone; the authoritative copy is the backend one, and this snippet has to be
# merged there so the next backend deploy does not overwrite it.
#
# Inserted INSIDE the existing `{$SITE_ADDRESS}` site block, after the
# /admin-preview handler and before the catch-all `reverse_proxy app:8080`.
#
# `handle`, NOT `handle_path`: the site is built with basePath=/web-preview, so
# Next expects to RECEIVE the prefix. Stripping it would 404 every page.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

	# Preview of the desktop guest site (apps/web in bookeat1/frontend). Unlike
	# /preview and /admin-preview this one is not a pile of files: it is a
	# Next.js server rendering on demand, so Caddy proxies instead of serving.
	#
	# The upstream is a container from a SEPARATE compose project
	# ("webpreview", /opt/bookeat/web-preview/docker-compose.yml) that joins
	# this stack's network. If it is down, only /web-preview answers 502; the
	# backend and the panel are unaffected.
	handle /web-preview* {
		reverse_proxy web-preview:3100
	}
